Modifications Copyright 2026 Oxynote

This package is a modified copy of the lezer-promql module from
https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus/tree/main/web/ui/module/lezer-promql
distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Everything not listed
below is upstream's, under The Prometheus Authors' copyright above.

Changes from upstream:

  - src/promql.grammar: added the DynamicDurationPlaceholder token and
    accepted it as a number, so duration placeholders ($__interval,
    $__range, $__rate_interval) parse as durations. Added the
    VariableReference token and accepted it as a number, a duration, a
    label name and a metric name.
    Added the metricsql dialect, which parses MetricsQL, the
    VictoriaMetrics query language: WITH templates, any-name function
    calls, the MetricsQL aggregations, limit, keep_metric_names, prefix,
    the if, ifnot and default operators, or between label filters, dotted
    metric names, empty windows, and MetricsQL numbers and durations.
  - src/tokens.js: added the MetricsQL keywords, aggregations, function
    names and label filter extras, which exist only while the metricsql
    dialect is on.
  - src/highlight.js: styled VariableReference as a special variable name,
    and styled the MetricsQL nodes like their PromQL counterparts.
  - test/expression.txt: parse cases for those placeholders and
    references.
  - test/metricsql.txt, test/promql.test.js: parse cases for the metricsql
    dialect, checks that PromQL still rejects them, and highlighting
    checks.

The metricsql dialect was written for this package. The constructs it
covers follow the MetricsQL documentation at
https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/metricsql/ and the
@cloudcare/lezer-metricsql grammar (Copyright (c) 2025 CloudCare, published
to npm under the MIT License, while its package.json declares Apache-2.0).
That grammar served as a reference only. No code is copied from it.
  - jest.config.cjs: dropped the ts-jest preset, which upstream resolves
    through the prometheus web/ui workspace.
  - generate-types.sh: names both copyright holders in the header it emits
    into the generated dist/index.d.ts.
  - NOTICE: trimmed to the components this package actually ships, as
    section 4(d) allows, and extended with the changes listed here.
  - package.json: renamed the package, pinned the package manager, and
    pointed the metadata at this repository.
  - .gitignore: stopped ignoring LICENSE, which is redistributed here.
  - README.md: describes the fork; SYNCING.md, sync-upstream.sh and
    .github/ are additions and contain no upstream code.

